 ## Subtopics
 
-### Alpha-Dissociated Packing
-Separates alpha from RGB and packs non-intersecting RGB textures. Reduces memory to ~45% of original but requires complex mask generation and packing algorithms [S1]. Choose when geometry can be cleanly split by transparency.
-
-### Multi-Channel Packing
-Packs multiple attributes (e.g., RGB + Alpha) into a single texture unit. Simple to implement but may waste bandwidth if channels are sparse [Parent]. Choose for simple, dense data.
+### [Parametric Texturing with Lightmap and Reference Map](20190-parametric-texturing-with-lightmap-and-reference-map.md)
+A texturing scheme for voxel landscapes that uses a single shader script for the entire landscape while storing varying parameters in separate arrays to avoid the memory overhead of per-voxel textures. It solves the problem of tiling and memory exhaustion in large voxel worlds by decoupling texture selection from the rendering loop, using a reference map to blend between two textures and a lightmap for shading. It is distinguished from per-voxel shader storage by its extreme inner-loop speed, despite offering limited blending ranges compared to more complex multi-texture approaches. Choose it when rendering large voxel landscapes with limited GPU memory and when inner-loop performance is critical. [20190-parametric-texturing-with-lightmap-and-reference-map.md]
 
